e minutes until it smells nutty  and it's nice and golden brown chicken  stock  we kind of want to gradually  incorporate this look at that it already  looks like gravy  let's add some more and kind of stir it  as we go  [Music]  so it's been a couple minutes this looks  really good see that it's gotten a  little bit thicker yeah  all right so she is ready so we are  gonna go in and add our chicken  oh  baby look at that it just makes me smile  oh my gosh we are going to base this  chicken  in this gravy oh my god my heart can't  take it we're going to smother this  chicken and all this delicious gravy  peppers onions flavor  [Music]  let's move on to our cabbage we're going  to add some oil to a pan again using  vegetable oil we have six slices of  bacon here red pepper  our onion  one small head of cabbage hair that i  have cored and shredded all right so  we're gonna let this wilt down a little  bit and then i'm gonna add some more in  and see how much i can fit  our cabbage is looking  so good so colorful i have to go  set up my table kind of nervous never  hosted kwanzaa  [Music]  all right well here it is my kwanzaa  spread i will admit i am pretty  impressed with myself let's call it  madison and hope she's just as impressed  as i am  hey madison how are you hi i'm doing  really well i'm excited to see what you  came up with did i do a good job oh wow  your smothered chicken looks really good  and your fried cabbage is perfectly  chopped so that's great i give you a 10  out of 10 i think it looks phenomenal  and how long does kwanzaa last i know  it's more than one day right so kwanzaa  actually starts on december 26th which  is the day after christmas and it goes  through january 1st and each of those  seven days is represented by a principle  of kwanzaa and why are these principles  important the seven principles of  kwanzaa are umoja hujichakulia ujima  ujama mia kumba and imani and these  translate to unity self-determination  collective work and responsi